WEBVTT

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:06.336
Captain's Log, Stardate 51367.2.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:09.467
We've spent the last three days
on the Mari homeworld.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.476
It's been a while
since we've had the opportunity

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.772
to make new friends

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:15.280
and the crew seems to be making
the most of our stay.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.210
Neelix.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.982
Tom. You've been doing
a little shopping.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.319
It's a present for B'Elanna.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.584
What is it?

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.024
Well, it's sort of personal.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.459
Of course.
Say no more.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:29.462
I'm on my way

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.158
for a little romantic
rendezvous myself.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.729
Neelix...

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.935
are you wearing cologne?

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.273
Oh...

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.005
Talchok musk.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.708
Very enticing scent,
don't you think?

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.444
Well, uh, it certainly is...

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.451
musky.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:55.477
I'm going to see Talli again.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.511
Ooh, that was fast work.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.614
Where're you taking her?

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.251
Well, actually, I haven't
gotten that far yet.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.954
I'm going to visit her shop,

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.623
under the pretext of buying
some produce for the ship,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:08.464
and then I thought I'd just
sort of segue smoothly

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.331
into some dinner and dancing.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.235
Sounds like a good strategy.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.467
You really think so?

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:18.204
I mean... you used to be
quite the ladies' man.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.211
"Used to be"?

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.406
Well, I mean,
you're involved now,

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.040
so, of course,
you won't be availing yourself

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.243
of all the beautiful,
fascinating

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.478
and very open-minded Mari women.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.146
Neelix, are you trying
to depress me?

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.712
I just...

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.917
I haven't been with anyone
since Kes

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.926
and I'm feeling a little rusty.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.485
I... I could use some advice.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.489
The best advice I can give you
is to just be yourself.

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.865
Right.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.368
Be myself.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:50.669
Actually... that's the
second-best piece of advice.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.699
What's the first?

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.680
Go a little easier on the musk.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.262
I'm sorry, Mr. Guill,
but that's my final offer.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.631
Actually, Captain,
I sense you'd be willing

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.262
to raise your price
to 300 renns.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.738
Lieutenant Torres needs
this resonator coil to upgrade

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.638
Voyager's
communications systems.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.903
Telepaths.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.910
Wait a minute.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.071
I sense you'd be willing to...

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.705
settle for 250.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.611
You must have read my mind.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.680
Hey!

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:35.710
I'm sorry.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.484
Are you hurt?

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.291
No, no, I'm fine.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.886
I just wish people would
look where they're going.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.454
It's been a pleasure
doing business with you.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.396
I'll finish up here.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.990
Why don't you go get Neelix?

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.837
All right.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.168
This is some
of the loveliest fruit

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.971
I've-I've seen in a long time.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:57.977
Actually, it's been

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:00.377
one of our worst
waterplum seasons in years.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.244
I don't think you'll
find them very sweet.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:08.085
Mmm. Mmm.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.281
Oh, how wonderfully tart.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.754
Mmm. They'll make
excellent preserves.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:15.351
Neelix?

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.327
Hmm?

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.454
Why do you want me

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:18.759
to tug on your whiskers?

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.428
Excu-excuse me?

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.458
That is what you're thinking,
isn't it...

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:26.438
that you'd like me
to tug on your whiskers?

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.805
Well, as a m-matter of fact...

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.673
I'd love to.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.508
Do you have time
to wait until I close?

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.546
Yes, I think
I can rearrange my schedule.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:46.319
I guess you could say
I'm becoming obsolete.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.656
In what sense?

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:51.425
There's virtually no crime
left in our society.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.056
It took many years,

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:55.158
but just walk
through our streets.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:56.293
Look around.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.327
Violence no longer exists.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.463
Impressive.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.235
I'm one of the last officers
still working

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.299
for the Constabulary.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.038
And no doubt one of the best.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:06.739
I'm curious to know more

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.247
about your
crime-prevention methods.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.874
Under one condition:

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:13.579
I want to see Voyager...
learn about your methods.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.453
I'm about to perform
my daily security rounds.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.023
Join me.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:19.752
They are routine
but informative.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.157
Wonderful.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.889
The transport site is this way.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.557
You prefer speaking aloud.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.860
Why is that?

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.925
I've grown accustomed
to it over the years.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:32.767
There are very few
telepaths in Starfleet.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.137
Whatever you prefer.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.800
Neelix...

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.334
ready to leave?

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.778
Uh, no, uh, you go ahead.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.247
I haven't finished
examining the produce.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.312
Help! Help!

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.377
Somebody help me, please!

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.888
Stop him!

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.658
Help me!

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.695
This will teach you to watch
where you're going, you idiot!

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:01.961
You idiot!

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.704
Somebody get a doctor!

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:10.441
Why?! Why were you
beating that man?

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.706
I don't know.

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:16.965
Your..."brig."
It's a puzzling concept...

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:20.199
shutting someone
away as punishment.

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:23.072
Do you find that it
rehabilitates the prisoner?

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:24.871
The brig is primarily used

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.310
as a means of ensuring
the safety of others.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:28.608
In what sense?

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.444
For example,
if we find ourselves

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.450
with a hostile alien
in our custody,

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:34.418
we may need
to confine the individual

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.284
until we can locate
the proper authorities.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.448
I see.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:39.081
And on rare occasions,
we have been forced

00:07:39.124 --> 00:07:40.455
to incarcerate a crew member

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.459
who has committed
a serious infraction.

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:45.224
I'm surprised
that one of your people

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.664
could be capable of doing
something serious enough

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.167
to warrant imprisonment.

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:50.668
It's extremely rare.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.603
In any case,
the brig has been occupied

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.697
for less than one percent
of our journey.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:59.040
Forgive me, Tuvok,
but it seems...

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:00.705
barbaric.

00:08:00.746 --> 00:08:01.838
If all species were

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.814
as enlightened
as yours and mine,

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:06.249
there would be no need
for prisons.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.775
Bridge to Commander Tuvok.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:08.878
Go ahead, Ensign.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:11.913
Chief Examiner Nimira's
been recalled to the surface.

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:15.256
There's been some sort of attack
in the marketplace.

00:08:19.631 --> 00:08:21.326
I've never seen
so much blood before.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.334
It's all right.

00:08:22.368 --> 00:08:24.563
I heard about someone
getting beaten once

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:25.592
when I was a little girl.

00:08:25.637 --> 00:08:26.604
It's all over now.

00:08:26.638 --> 00:08:27.764
I had nightmares for weeks.

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:30.001
It's okay.
It's all right.

00:08:31.443 --> 00:08:33.070
He was confused.

00:08:33.112 --> 00:08:35.307
He said he didn't realize
what he'd done.

00:08:35.347 --> 00:08:37.406
I don't understand
why nobody tried to help him.

00:08:37.449 --> 00:08:39.440
People were shocked.

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:41.453
Violence is
almost unheard of here.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.613
But when it does occur,

00:08:43.655 --> 00:08:45.418
we like
to investigate thoroughly.

00:08:45.457 --> 00:08:46.446
Can we help?

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:47.618
Yes. I would

00:08:47.659 --> 00:08:50.150
like you, Mr. Neelix
and, uh, Lieutenant Torres

00:08:50.195 --> 00:08:52.129
to answer some questions.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:54.098
Well, you have
our complete cooperation.

00:08:54.133 --> 00:08:56.101
Chief Examiner,
are you suspicious

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:58.069
of my colleagues
for some reason?

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.297
No, Lieutenant.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.636
I'm simply conducting
an investigation.

00:09:01.673 --> 00:09:03.664
Please.
Follow me.

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.088
Please have a seat.

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:24.160
I will be monitoring
your thoughts telepathically

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:25.424
during the interview.

00:09:25.497 --> 00:09:26.964
This transcription device

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:28.933
will log
your engramatic activity,

00:09:28.967 --> 00:09:30.832
so I can review
your statement later.

00:09:30.869 --> 00:09:32.427
Let me get this straight.

00:09:32.538 --> 00:09:35.769
Not only are you going
to read my mind,

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:37.435
you're going
to record my thoughts.

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:38.841
Yes.

00:09:38.877 --> 00:09:42.938
I guess it'd be pretty tough
to keep a secret from you, hmm?

00:09:53.358 --> 00:09:55.326
How long had you been
in the marketplace

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.657
when the attack occurred?

00:09:56.695 --> 00:09:59.391
One hour...
maybe a little longer.

00:09:59.431 --> 00:10:01.695
And exactly where
were you standing?

00:10:01.733 --> 00:10:04.099
Directly across the square.

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.661
From where you were, did you
have a clear view of the attack?

00:10:06.705 --> 00:10:09.071
Uh, not at first.

00:10:09.107 --> 00:10:10.369
We just heard yelling.

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:11.842
Then, as we got closer,

00:10:11.877 --> 00:10:13.469
we saw what was happening.

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:14.638
What exactly brought you

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.238
to the market
in the first place?

00:10:16.281 --> 00:10:18.044
Captain Janeway and I

00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:19.914
had an appointment
with Mr. Guill.

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:21.180
For what purpose?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.983
We'd met him the day before.

00:10:23.021 --> 00:10:25.683
He said he could get
a spare resonator coil for us.

00:10:25.724 --> 00:10:26.816
I see.

00:10:26.859 --> 00:10:28.986
And the two men involved
in the altercation...

00:10:29.027 --> 00:10:30.392
had you seen either of them
before?

00:10:30.429 --> 00:10:32.989
I'd never seen the victim...

00:10:33.031 --> 00:10:35.499
but the attacker...

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:39.003
I think he was the same man
who bumped into B'Elanna.

00:10:39.037 --> 00:10:40.595
Bumped into her?

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:41.970
Are you certain?

00:10:42.007 --> 00:10:43.998
Yes. They collided accidentally.

00:10:45.544 --> 00:10:48.104
When exactly did this happen?

00:10:48.146 --> 00:10:50.410
Just as we'd settled
on the price.

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:52.280
He seemed to be
in quite a hurry.

00:10:52.317 --> 00:10:54.945
Do you recall what you
were thinking at the time?

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:56.352
What I was thinking?

00:10:56.388 --> 00:10:57.514
What does it matter?

00:10:57.589 --> 00:10:58.521
Please...

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.057
try to remember.

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:01.389
It may be important.

00:11:01.426 --> 00:11:03.360
I didn't think about it much

00:11:03.395 --> 00:11:05.295
and no one was hurt,
and I was busy

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.991
trying to sort out the coins.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:09.193
I'm not used
to handling currency.

00:11:09.234 --> 00:11:10.599
What was I thinking?

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.939
I was thinking how I could bake
a delicious pie

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:16.440
with those waterplums.

00:11:16.475 --> 00:11:19.239
Are you sure that's all,
Mr. Neelix?

00:11:19.278 --> 00:11:21.246
Yes, of course.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:24.408
What else would I
be thinking about?

00:11:24.449 --> 00:11:27.145
I suppose I was
a little annoyed.

00:11:27.185 --> 00:11:29.278
Can you be more specific?

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:31.118
All right.

00:11:31.156 --> 00:11:34.751
I guess I was thinking
my foot hurt.

00:11:34.793 --> 00:11:36.488
I mean, the idiot stepped
right on it.

00:11:36.528 --> 00:11:38.462
Did you call him an idiot?

00:11:38.497 --> 00:11:39.486
Of course not.

00:11:39.531 --> 00:11:40.896
But you thought it?

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:42.833
I guess so.

00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:44.768
Did you also think
about retaliating?

00:11:44.803 --> 00:11:46.737
It was an accident.

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:48.433
But you said he hurt you.

00:11:48.473 --> 00:11:50.634
It didn't occur to you
to hurt him back?

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:51.768
I'd never do that.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.938
But you thought about it.

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:58.449
How am I supposed to remember?

00:11:58.483 --> 00:12:01.919
Yes or no,
did you think about hurting him?

00:12:03.822 --> 00:12:05.653
Yes or no?!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.860
Well, maybe for a split second.

00:12:11.897 --> 00:12:13.262
Hey!

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:16.664
I mean, he should
have been watching

00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:17.669
where he was going,

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:20.035
but I realized
that he didn't do it on purpose

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:21.039
so I shook it off

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:23.132
and I left.

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.267
Why?

00:12:24.309 --> 00:12:27.107
What does it matter
what I was thinking?

00:12:29.314 --> 00:12:32.340
Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres,
you are under arrest.

00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:34.648
On what charge?!

00:12:34.686 --> 00:12:39.020
Aggravated violent thought
resulting in grave bodily harm.

00:12:46.064 --> 00:12:49.261
Are you saying it's a crime
to think about violence?

00:12:49.301 --> 00:12:50.268
Yes.

00:12:50.302 --> 00:12:51.269
That's ridiculous.

00:12:51.303 --> 00:12:53.897
I assure you,
it's quite necessary.

00:12:53.939 --> 00:12:57.204
We were once a society
plagued by violence.

00:12:57.242 --> 00:12:59.210
When we prohibited
hostile thought,

00:12:59.244 --> 00:13:01.769
crime began to drop immediately.

00:13:01.814 --> 00:13:05.682
Over the past three generations,
it's all but disappeared.

00:13:05.717 --> 00:13:07.082
So you believe
that it's all right

00:13:07.119 --> 00:13:10.282
to tell people what they
can and cannot think?

00:13:10.322 --> 00:13:11.880
It's an irrefutable fact

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:13.915
that violent thoughts
from others

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.450
can lead to violent actions.

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:19.395
Even if B'Elanna had
a violent thought,

00:13:19.431 --> 00:13:22.127
it was Frane
who attacked that man.

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:24.897
Which he only did
because he telepathically

00:13:24.937 --> 00:13:26.871
received that thought
from B'Elanna.

00:13:26.905 --> 00:13:29.396
His mind was contaminated
by the image,

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.636
and it resulted
in a loss of control.

00:13:31.677 --> 00:13:33.440
He may have committed
the physical act,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:36.209
but it was instigated by you.

00:13:36.248 --> 00:13:37.215
Where we come from,

00:13:37.249 --> 00:13:40.047
people are responsible
for their own actions.

00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:42.781
And here,
people are responsible

00:13:42.821 --> 00:13:44.812
for their own thoughts.

00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:48.224
I'm sure you can understand
how that's necessary for a race

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.488
of telepaths.

00:13:49.561 --> 00:13:51.051
Yes, I can.

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:52.154
Captain!

00:13:52.197 --> 00:13:53.664
I'll accept that your people

00:13:53.699 --> 00:13:56.133
can be influenced
by the thoughts of others,

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:59.160
but there were dozens
of people in that square.

00:13:59.204 --> 00:14:01.536
How can you be certain
it came from B'Elanna?

00:14:01.573 --> 00:14:04.701
The Mari no longer have
violent thoughts.

00:14:04.743 --> 00:14:08.372
It's unlikely any of them
could have been responsible.

00:14:08.413 --> 00:14:11.678
Besides, the evidence
against B'Elanna is clear.

00:14:11.717 --> 00:14:14.242
She thought about
committing a hostile act.

00:14:14.286 --> 00:14:16.186
I'd like to review
that evidence myself,

00:14:16.221 --> 00:14:17.347
if you don't mind.

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:19.152
Certainly.

00:14:19.191 --> 00:14:22.183
But I'm afraid
you'll be disappointed.

00:14:23.929 --> 00:14:25.794
What happens to B'Elanna now?

00:14:25.831 --> 00:14:29.164
We have an enlightened
penal system here.

00:14:29.201 --> 00:14:33.001
Unlike some, we don't lock
people away to punish them.

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:35.097
You'll be released...

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.768
once you've undergone
the engramatic purge.

00:14:37.809 --> 00:14:38.776
The what?

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:39.936
It's a medical

00:14:39.978 --> 00:14:42.173
procedure that will
identify and remove

00:14:42.214 --> 00:14:44.273
the offending images
from your mind.

00:14:44.316 --> 00:14:45.783
Captain!

00:14:45.817 --> 00:14:47.079
Once identified,

00:14:47.119 --> 00:14:51.112
the images can be removed
from Frane's mind as well.

00:14:51.156 --> 00:14:52.817
Memory extraction...

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:55.088
that's a dangerous procedure.

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:58.688
There is a risk
of neurological damage,

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:02.632
but it's necessary
for us to treat Frane.

00:15:04.169 --> 00:15:06.228
Will you at least
delay the procedure

00:15:06.271 --> 00:15:09.069
until we've had a chance
to review the evidence?

00:15:09.107 --> 00:15:10.734
Will you?

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:17.443
Lt'll take us about a day
to reconfigure our instruments.

00:15:17.482 --> 00:15:20.713
That's all the time
I can give you.

00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:24.252
That's all the time
I'll need.

00:15:49.848 --> 00:15:50.906
Captain,

00:15:50.949 --> 00:15:52.246
we've got to get
B'Elanna out of there.

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:53.376
You know the rules, Tom.

00:15:53.418 --> 00:15:54.578
We can't pick and choose

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.815
which laws we'll respect
and which we won't.

00:15:56.855 --> 00:15:59.483
Nobody can be expected
to control their thoughts.

00:15:59.524 --> 00:16:00.752
Tell that to the Mari.

00:16:00.792 --> 00:16:03.522
Are you just going to let them
put her through this process?

00:16:03.562 --> 00:16:05.291
I'm doing everything
I can to stop it.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.423
Neelix is going to file
a diplomatic protest

00:16:07.532 --> 00:16:10.330
and Tuvok and I will be going
over the witness statements.

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:13.395
Maybe we can poke a few holes
in the Chief Examiner's case.

00:16:13.438 --> 00:16:14.564
And if you can't?

00:16:15.607 --> 00:16:17.802
Then let's hope
the Doctor can figure out

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:19.743
how to reverse
an engramatic purge.

00:16:22.047 --> 00:16:23.571
All away personnel
have been notified

00:16:23.615 --> 00:16:25.412
to return to the ship
as soon as possible.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.008
So much for R&amp;R.

00:16:28.453 --> 00:16:30.921
Chakotay, we've got to talk.

00:16:30.956 --> 00:16:32.014
Have a seat.

00:16:32.057 --> 00:16:34.025
Here?

00:16:34.059 --> 00:16:36.391
I'm sure the Captain
wouldn't object.

00:16:36.428 --> 00:16:38.919
What's on your mind?

00:16:38.964 --> 00:16:41.296
While Tuvok and the Captain
are reviewing the evidence,

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.392
B'Elanna's sitting
in a Mari jail cell

00:16:43.435 --> 00:16:45.062
waiting
for some sort of lobotomy.

00:16:45.103 --> 00:16:46.127
We can't let that happen.

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:47.263
What did you have in mind?

00:16:47.305 --> 00:16:48.465
Break her out.

00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:51.374
And risk an all-out
confrontation with the Mari?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:52.877
They're a bunch of pacifists.

00:16:52.911 --> 00:16:54.139
They're no match for us.

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:56.010
You're probably right,

00:16:56.048 --> 00:16:58.414
but before we start resorting
to extreme measures,

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.475
don't you think we should give
the Captain a chance

00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:01.747
to find a legal solution?

00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:04.153
By the time that happens,
it may be too late.

00:17:04.189 --> 00:17:05.918
I'll tell you what.

00:17:05.957 --> 00:17:08.255
Why don't you come up
with a rescue plan...

00:17:08.293 --> 00:17:10.921
one that minimizes
the possibility of violence...

00:17:10.962 --> 00:17:12.020
and I'll review it.

00:17:12.064 --> 00:17:14.328
You're just trying
to keep me busy, aren't you?

00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:16.425
Can you blame me?

00:17:16.501 --> 00:17:18.435
I'm serious about this,
Chakotay.

00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.301
So am I.
If your plan is sound,

00:17:20.338 --> 00:17:23.307
and the Captain doesn't have
any luck on her end,

00:17:23.341 --> 00:17:25.002
I'll recommend we attempt
the rescue.

00:17:25.043 --> 00:17:26.670
Thanks.

00:17:26.712 --> 00:17:28.441
I'll get right on it.

00:17:28.547 --> 00:17:29.707
Tom...

00:17:29.748 --> 00:17:31.943
I may have let you sit
in the Captain's chair,

00:17:31.983 --> 00:17:34.281
but remember,
she's still the boss.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:41.450
Then you don't accept
the Chief Examiner's conclusion?

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:42.618
I'm not dismissing it,

00:17:42.661 --> 00:17:45.357
but I'm not going
to accept it blindly either.

00:17:45.397 --> 00:17:47.365
I've spent a great deal of time

00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:49.697
with Nimira
over the past few days.

00:17:49.735 --> 00:17:52.704
She clearly is
a very skilled investigator.

00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:54.069
I'm sure she is.

00:17:54.106 --> 00:17:55.437
And this isn't the first time

00:17:55.474 --> 00:17:57.305
Lieutenant Torres'
violent proclivities

00:17:57.342 --> 00:17:58.900
have created problems.

00:17:58.944 --> 00:18:00.468
No argument there.

00:18:00.512 --> 00:18:02.639
But I have a hard time buying

00:18:02.681 --> 00:18:06.276
that one fleeting thought
makes her responsible

00:18:06.318 --> 00:18:07.649
for a vicious attack.

00:18:07.686 --> 00:18:10.553
From what I've learned,
crime here is a result

00:18:10.589 --> 00:18:12.523
of exposure
to violent thought,

00:18:12.557 --> 00:18:14.422
much as it was on Vulcan

00:18:14.493 --> 00:18:17.155
before my people learned
to control their emotions.

00:18:17.195 --> 00:18:19.925
In my opinion,
the Mari should be

00:18:19.965 --> 00:18:21.432
applauded for their efforts.

00:18:21.466 --> 00:18:24.196
Oh, I'm sure their intentions
are admirable, but, uh...

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:27.137
I'm not about to let them
scramble B'Elanna's brain

00:18:27.172 --> 00:18:28.332
without a fight.

00:18:28.373 --> 00:18:30.637
But we must prepare ourselves
for the probability

00:18:30.675 --> 00:18:32.404
that she will turn out
to be culpable

00:18:32.444 --> 00:18:33.775
for the crime.

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:35.575
Maybe so...

00:18:35.614 --> 00:18:37.946
and then again...

00:18:37.983 --> 00:18:39.780
maybe not.

00:18:39.818 --> 00:18:41.581
Take a look at this.

00:18:43.221 --> 00:18:45.587
I don't mean to accuse
your friend Nimira

00:18:45.624 --> 00:18:47.649
of being less than thorough,
Tuvok,

00:18:47.692 --> 00:18:51.025
but don't you find that
just the least bit curious?

00:18:54.132 --> 00:18:56.066
"New evidence"?

00:18:56.101 --> 00:18:59.036
It concerns the attacker,
Mr. Frane.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.197
According to your own
security records,

00:19:01.239 --> 00:19:03.366
he was arrested on
four previous occasions

00:19:03.408 --> 00:19:04.773
for harboring violent thoughts.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.300
You classified him

00:19:06.344 --> 00:19:09.643
as an "habitual perpetrator
of hostile images."

00:19:09.681 --> 00:19:10.841
True.

00:19:10.882 --> 00:19:14.215
But those thoughts
were purged each time.

00:19:14.252 --> 00:19:17.688
He spent years
in neurogenic restructuring.

00:19:17.722 --> 00:19:20.748
The records also
say he was cured.

00:19:20.792 --> 00:19:24.694
Still, it is possible
that Frane had a relapse...

00:19:24.729 --> 00:19:26.094
that he alone is responsible

00:19:26.131 --> 00:19:27.860
for his actions
at the marketplace.

00:19:27.899 --> 00:19:31.300
Possible, but unlikely.

00:19:31.336 --> 00:19:34.635
Our engramatic scans of Frane

00:19:34.673 --> 00:19:37.904
show that Lieutenant
Torres's thought

00:19:37.943 --> 00:19:41.003
was prevalent in his mind
during the attack.

00:19:41.046 --> 00:19:43.571
And you are certain

00:19:43.615 --> 00:19:45.640
no other violent
thoughts were present?

00:19:45.684 --> 00:19:47.845
I'm beginning to feel

00:19:47.886 --> 00:19:49.786
like I'm the one
being investigated.

00:19:49.821 --> 00:19:52.722
I am simply exploring
all logical options.

00:19:52.757 --> 00:19:54.588
As a fellow
law enforcement officer,

00:19:54.626 --> 00:19:56.025
you should understand that.

00:19:56.061 --> 00:19:58.461
I do.

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:02.466
And I'm willing to share
my findings with you.

00:20:02.567 --> 00:20:04.228
But if you're trying to prove

00:20:04.269 --> 00:20:09.002
your crewmate's innocence,
you're too late.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:12.032
The case is closed.

00:20:16.114 --> 00:20:18.344
Do you think
that this is easy for me?

00:20:18.383 --> 00:20:22.479
I don't want to harm B'Elanna,
but I don't have a choice.

00:20:22.587 --> 00:20:24.885
That thought has
to be contained.

00:20:24.923 --> 00:20:27.483
Otherwise, we risk
further violence, maybe even

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:29.288
a citywide panic.

00:20:29.327 --> 00:20:31.921
You told me your people
spent centuries

00:20:31.963 --> 00:20:35.160
learning how to control
their violent impulses.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:38.192
I know we haven't achieved
your level of discipline,

00:20:38.236 --> 00:20:40.101
but we're trying.

00:20:41.473 --> 00:20:43.441
I thought you'd understand.

00:20:45.443 --> 00:20:47.638
I am not judging your culture.

00:20:47.679 --> 00:20:50.443
In fact, I admire it.

00:20:50.482 --> 00:20:53.883
I have enjoyed
your company in particular,

00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:58.515
but I cannot abandon
my responsibility to B'Elanna.

00:20:58.623 --> 00:21:02.081
I must continue
my own investigation.

00:21:02.127 --> 00:21:04.357
Go right ahead.

00:21:04.396 --> 00:21:07.456
But I intend to proceed
with the engramatic purge.

00:21:11.369 --> 00:21:13.234
Telepathy...

00:21:13.271 --> 00:21:15.262
I don't like it.
Never have.

00:21:15.307 --> 00:21:17.275
It's bad for negotiations,

00:21:17.309 --> 00:21:19.004
it's bad for relationships

00:21:19.044 --> 00:21:21.877
and it's certainly
been bad for B'Elanna.

00:21:21.913 --> 00:21:24.006
The fault was her own.

00:21:24.049 --> 00:21:25.812
What are you talking about?

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:28.182
She was careless
with her thoughts.

00:21:28.219 --> 00:21:29.982
The result was violence.

00:21:30.021 --> 00:21:33.013
B'Elanna's not used
to being around telepaths.

00:21:33.058 --> 00:21:34.719
That doesn't make her guilty.

00:21:34.759 --> 00:21:36.954
Then her crime was ignorance...

00:21:36.995 --> 00:21:39.429
a common affliction
among your crew.

00:21:40.465 --> 00:21:41.955
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.865
You make contact
with alien species

00:21:43.902 --> 00:21:46.598
without sufficient understanding
of their nature.

00:21:46.638 --> 00:21:50.631
As a result, Voyager's directive
to "seek out new civilizations"

00:21:50.675 --> 00:21:52.267
often ends in conflict.

00:21:54.546 --> 00:21:59.210
What you call "ignorance,"
we call "exploration..."

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:02.447
and sometimes it means
taking a few risks.

00:22:02.554 --> 00:22:05.455
But it's certainly better
than assimilating

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:06.548
everything in your path.

00:22:06.591 --> 00:22:08.889
Your goal is to share knowledge.

00:22:08.927 --> 00:22:11.862
Assimilation is the perfect
means of attaining that goal.

00:22:13.264 --> 00:22:15.391
"Perfect."

00:22:15.433 --> 00:22:17.060
Good morning, Miss Tembit.

00:22:17.102 --> 00:22:18.467
Your usual selection?

00:22:18.536 --> 00:22:19.468
Yes, please.

00:22:19.537 --> 00:22:20.469
Okay.

00:22:20.538 --> 00:22:22.699
Oh, I'm-I'm so sorry.

00:22:22.741 --> 00:22:24.470
Hey!

00:22:24.542 --> 00:22:26.510
Idiot!
Watch what you're doing!

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:50.528
She's dead.

00:22:56.239 --> 00:22:58.605
I can't believe she's dead.

00:22:58.642 --> 00:23:00.974
I know this is difficult
for you, Mr. Neelix,

00:23:01.011 --> 00:23:03.639
but try to recount for me
everything that happened.

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:07.241
Seven and I were packing
to return to the ship.

00:23:07.284 --> 00:23:08.546
We heard a scream.

00:23:08.585 --> 00:23:09.813
I went running...

00:23:09.853 --> 00:23:13.050
The old lady was just
standing over Talli's body,

00:23:13.090 --> 00:23:15.650
holding the bloody knife
in her hand.

00:23:15.692 --> 00:23:18.661
I didn't even get a chance
to say good-bye.

00:23:18.695 --> 00:23:20.754
Did the old woman say anything?

00:23:20.797 --> 00:23:22.355
Not that I remember.

00:23:22.399 --> 00:23:25.163
She was as shocked and confused
as anyone else.

00:23:26.837 --> 00:23:29.203
Do you think this
is somehow connected

00:23:29.239 --> 00:23:30.672
with the other attack?

00:23:30.707 --> 00:23:32.140
I'm not certain,

00:23:32.175 --> 00:23:34.473
but it strikes me
as more than coincidence

00:23:34.511 --> 00:23:37.480
that two violent altercations
have occurred within two days,

00:23:37.581 --> 00:23:38.912
in a city which purports

00:23:38.949 --> 00:23:41.076
to have eliminated
virtually all crime.

00:23:41.118 --> 00:23:42.881
Bridge to Commander Tuvok.

00:23:42.919 --> 00:23:44.113
Tuvok here.

00:23:44.154 --> 00:23:46.486
Chief Examiner Nimira
wants to see you.

00:23:46.556 --> 00:23:49.286
She's requesting permission
to transport aboard.

00:23:49.326 --> 00:23:50.884
Permission granted.

00:23:50.927 --> 00:23:52.690
Have her escorted
to the briefing room.

00:23:52.729 --> 00:23:53.957
Tuvok out.

00:23:53.997 --> 00:23:55.988
We will continue later.

00:23:56.032 --> 00:23:57.897
Commander.

00:23:59.536 --> 00:24:01.401
She was a wonderful young woman.

00:24:01.438 --> 00:24:05.340
Whoever's responsible
for her death... find them,

00:24:05.375 --> 00:24:07.206
and see that they're
brought to justice.

00:24:07.244 --> 00:24:09.542
I will do my best, Mr. Neelix.

00:24:32.269 --> 00:24:34.066
Thanks for seeing me.

00:24:34.104 --> 00:24:35.696
I heard what happened.

00:24:35.739 --> 00:24:38.970
Do you have any idea what
caused this latest attack?

00:24:39.009 --> 00:24:41.842
I just finished interviewing
the old woman.

00:24:41.878 --> 00:24:43.243
And?

00:24:43.280 --> 00:24:44.713
She attacked the victim

00:24:44.748 --> 00:24:46.875
in response to the
same violent thought

00:24:46.917 --> 00:24:48.782
that motivated
the previous beating.

00:24:48.819 --> 00:24:49.945
B'Elanna's thought?

00:24:51.121 --> 00:24:53.419
But both she and Frane
are in custody.

00:24:53.456 --> 00:24:55.947
How could the thought
have been passed to anyone else?

00:24:55.992 --> 00:24:57.789
I don't know.

00:24:57.828 --> 00:25:00.160
That's why I'm here.

00:25:00.197 --> 00:25:03.030
I need your help.

00:25:04.901 --> 00:25:06.095
Then you shall have it.

00:25:06.136 --> 00:25:08.366
Thank you.

00:25:08.405 --> 00:25:11.806
I don't know why that thought
is still contaminating people,

00:25:11.842 --> 00:25:13.867
but I have got
to put a stop to it.

00:25:13.910 --> 00:25:15.537
I've never dealt
with a murder before,

00:25:15.579 --> 00:25:19.174
but you've had experience
with homicide investigations?

00:25:19.216 --> 00:25:20.683
I have.

00:25:20.717 --> 00:25:22.241
I thought I would start
by tracing

00:25:22.285 --> 00:25:24.549
the old woman's whereabouts
for the past few days

00:25:24.588 --> 00:25:26.647
to see where she might have
encountered the thought.

00:25:26.690 --> 00:25:28.282
A wise choice.

00:25:28.325 --> 00:25:30.020
In the meantime, I would like

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:31.994
to interview B'Elanna
more extensively.

00:25:32.028 --> 00:25:33.427
Perhaps a fresh perspective

00:25:33.463 --> 00:25:35.693
might uncover facts
you hadn't considered.

00:25:35.732 --> 00:25:37.632
I'll arrange it immediately.

00:25:44.774 --> 00:25:47.242
I'm not sure I like
the idea of a mind-meld

00:25:47.277 --> 00:25:49.108
any better
than an engramatic purge.

00:25:49.145 --> 00:25:51.375
It will be a limited meld.

00:25:51.414 --> 00:25:53.609
I will focus exclusively
on your memories

00:25:53.650 --> 00:25:55.743
of the events
surrounding the crime.

00:25:55.785 --> 00:25:58.151
It poses no danger.

00:25:58.188 --> 00:25:59.780
Are you ready?

00:26:06.930 --> 00:26:09.330
Your mind to my mind.

00:26:09.366 --> 00:26:12.858
Your thoughts to my thoughts.

00:26:12.903 --> 00:26:16.600
Recall your encounter
with Mr. Frane.

00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:18.232
He bumped into you.

00:26:18.275 --> 00:26:19.902
What happened next?

00:26:19.943 --> 00:26:21.968
I guess that's
when I had the thought

00:26:22.012 --> 00:26:23.104
about hitting him.

00:26:23.146 --> 00:26:24.170
And after that?

00:26:24.214 --> 00:26:26.944
Guill came over
and asked if I was hurt.

00:26:26.983 --> 00:26:29.645
And what were you thinking
at that moment?

00:26:29.686 --> 00:26:30.880
Why?

00:26:30.921 --> 00:26:33.913
I'm sensing something
more to the encounter

00:26:33.957 --> 00:26:35.447
than what you've told me.

00:26:35.492 --> 00:26:37.357
Try to recall.

00:26:37.394 --> 00:26:38.986
It may be important.

00:26:39.029 --> 00:26:42.123
Well, he was just holding me
by the shoulders.

00:26:42.165 --> 00:26:44.395
You said he'd been
reading your mind

00:26:44.434 --> 00:26:46.402
during the negotiation.

00:26:46.436 --> 00:26:48.097
Was he still doing it?

00:26:48.138 --> 00:26:49.196
I don't know.

00:26:49.239 --> 00:26:51.764
You experienced
negative feelings about him.

00:26:53.543 --> 00:26:55.067
He gave me the creeps.

00:26:55.111 --> 00:26:56.703
In what sense?

00:26:57.614 --> 00:27:00.310
He... wanted something.

00:27:00.350 --> 00:27:02.818
Something terrible.

00:27:02.852 --> 00:27:04.513
What the hell?

00:27:06.389 --> 00:27:09.119
Why didn't I
remember that before?

00:27:09.159 --> 00:27:10.251
You may be recalling

00:27:10.293 --> 00:27:12.420
an unconscious thought
you had at the time

00:27:12.462 --> 00:27:14.123
or an intuition.

00:27:14.164 --> 00:27:17.327
Perhaps I should ask Mr. Guill.

00:27:26.276 --> 00:27:27.868
Mr. Guill.

00:27:31.114 --> 00:27:32.308
I'm Commander Tuvok,

00:27:32.349 --> 00:27:33.816
Voyager's Chief of Security.

00:27:33.850 --> 00:27:36.785
My children get upset
when I'm late for supper.

00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:38.082
If you're here to do business,

00:27:38.121 --> 00:27:39.952
we could make an appointment
for tomorrow.

00:27:39.990 --> 00:27:42.458
I'm here to talk to you
about the attack.

00:27:42.525 --> 00:27:44.049
Why me?

00:27:44.094 --> 00:27:45.459
My crewmate, Lieutenant Torres

00:27:45.528 --> 00:27:47.655
has been charged with the crime.

00:27:47.697 --> 00:27:49.358
I believe
you're acquainted with her.

00:27:49.399 --> 00:27:51.458
Lieutenant Torres, yes.

00:27:51.501 --> 00:27:53.025
She was arrested?

00:27:53.069 --> 00:27:55.970
The Chief Examiner believes
it was her violent thought,

00:27:56.006 --> 00:27:57.473
which prompted the beating.

00:27:57.507 --> 00:27:59.941
She seemed like such
a pleasant young woman.

00:28:02.912 --> 00:28:04.743
Apparently, she was
almost knocked over

00:28:04.781 --> 00:28:06.214
while doing business with you.

00:28:06.249 --> 00:28:07.876
Do you recall that?

00:28:07.917 --> 00:28:09.145
Yes.

00:28:09.185 --> 00:28:11.176
A man accidentally
ran into her and...

00:28:14.691 --> 00:28:17.785
You're not like the others
from your ship, are you?

00:28:17.827 --> 00:28:19.727
You're a telepath.

00:28:19.763 --> 00:28:21.287
That is correct.

00:28:22.532 --> 00:28:24.295
Why are you so curious
about what happened?

00:28:24.334 --> 00:28:27.303
I am conducting my own
investigation of the crime.

00:28:27.337 --> 00:28:29.305
I see.

00:28:29.339 --> 00:28:33.207
For a moment, I thought you had
another reason for asking.

00:28:33.243 --> 00:28:38.078
You... struggle
with violent thoughts as well.

00:28:38.114 --> 00:28:40.844
Terrible images,
but they're hidden

00:28:40.884 --> 00:28:42.317
deep within your mind.

00:28:42.352 --> 00:28:45.014
I am in control of those images.

00:28:45.055 --> 00:28:48.582
All members of the Vulcan race
learn to inhibit emotions.

00:28:48.625 --> 00:28:51.059
If my unconscious thoughts
are disturbing you,

00:28:51.094 --> 00:28:53.426
I will attempt to suppress
them further.

00:28:53.463 --> 00:28:54.452
No, please.

00:28:54.497 --> 00:28:57.193
Don't trouble yourself.

00:28:57.233 --> 00:28:59.326
I can't see them clearly enough
to be affected.

00:29:00.737 --> 00:29:04.935
I sense that you are fascinated
with my unconscious thoughts.

00:29:04.974 --> 00:29:07.943
That you would like to see
more of them if you could.

00:29:07.977 --> 00:29:09.672
No.

00:29:09.712 --> 00:29:13.773
I was just thinking
maybe I could help you.

00:29:13.817 --> 00:29:15.045
Help me?

00:29:15.085 --> 00:29:17.952
In learning how to deal
with these...

00:29:17.987 --> 00:29:19.215
dark impulses.

00:29:19.255 --> 00:29:21.086
No, thank you.

00:29:21.124 --> 00:29:23.422
I have sufficient means
of controlling them.

00:29:23.460 --> 00:29:25.223
I'm sure you do.

00:29:32.335 --> 00:29:34.428
Any other questions?

00:29:34.471 --> 00:29:36.598
No.

00:29:36.639 --> 00:29:38.038
Then, if you'll excuse me,

00:29:38.074 --> 00:29:40.099
I really can't be late
for the table.

00:30:08.338 --> 00:30:09.635
Do you have the money?

00:30:09.672 --> 00:30:10.934
3,000 renns.

00:30:17.814 --> 00:30:20.374
I have something
exciting for you tonight.

00:30:37.534 --> 00:30:39.502
Why are you following us?

00:30:39.536 --> 00:30:42.369
I was thinking
about what you said...

00:30:42.405 --> 00:30:45.203
your interest
in my unconscious thoughts.

00:30:45.241 --> 00:30:47.937
Perhaps we could
help each other.

00:30:47.977 --> 00:30:50.172
How would we do that?

00:30:50.213 --> 00:30:53.649
By telepathically exchanging
violent images.

00:30:53.683 --> 00:30:55.514
That is
what you want, isn't it?

00:30:55.618 --> 00:30:58.712
To see what's
buried in my unconscious?

00:30:58.755 --> 00:31:00.313
Who is he?

00:31:00.356 --> 00:31:01.823
Quiet.

00:31:01.858 --> 00:31:03.985
Why should I trust you?

00:31:04.027 --> 00:31:08.623
Because you know
we are very much alike.

00:31:10.867 --> 00:31:13.301
Perhaps I was mistaken.

00:31:13.336 --> 00:31:14.564
Wait.

00:31:19.576 --> 00:31:22.340
Maybe we can be of use
to each other.

00:31:22.378 --> 00:31:24.209
But you'll have
to get rid of this.

00:31:32.722 --> 00:31:34.747
Come back later, Malin.

00:31:34.791 --> 00:31:37.191
If I'm right,
I'll have thoughts to share

00:31:37.227 --> 00:31:39.388
that are darker
than anything you can imagine.

00:32:07.923 --> 00:32:09.720
Well?

00:32:09.759 --> 00:32:11.226
Fascinating.

00:32:12.194 --> 00:32:14.458
Now...

00:32:14.563 --> 00:32:15.757
show me.

00:32:16.832 --> 00:32:18.925
I'll need a few moments
to recover.

00:32:20.836 --> 00:32:22.929
I'm surprised
you're so easily tired.

00:32:22.972 --> 00:32:25.463
Your telepathic abilities
are strong.

00:32:25.541 --> 00:32:28.510
It is not often that I
exercise those skills.

00:32:29.845 --> 00:32:32.712
There must be violent thoughts
to be had from your shipmates,

00:32:32.748 --> 00:32:35.979
whether they want
to share them or not.

00:32:36.018 --> 00:32:40.011
After all, they
couldn't stop a telepath

00:32:40.056 --> 00:32:42.251
from probing their minds,
could they?

00:32:42.291 --> 00:32:44.851
Is that how you acquire
your merchandise?

00:32:45.861 --> 00:32:47.920
Sometimes I buy.

00:32:47.963 --> 00:32:49.624
Sometimes I find
a person like you

00:32:49.665 --> 00:32:50.859
who's willing to share,

00:32:50.900 --> 00:32:52.731
and, yes, when the opportunity
presents itself,

00:32:52.768 --> 00:32:54.668
I take what I need.

00:32:54.704 --> 00:32:57.434
Which is what you did
to Lieutenant Torres.

00:32:57.473 --> 00:33:01.432
Frane took her thought,
not me.

00:33:03.112 --> 00:33:04.579
So, you know Mr. Frane.

00:33:04.613 --> 00:33:06.706
Only casually.

00:33:06.749 --> 00:33:08.444
Well enough
to be in business with him?

00:33:08.484 --> 00:33:09.712
Why do you ask?

00:33:09.752 --> 00:33:12.277
I am interested in the thought
he acquired from B'Elanna...

00:33:12.321 --> 00:33:15.620
her violent tendencies
have always fascinated me,

00:33:15.658 --> 00:33:19.025
yet I've never succeeded
in probing her mind.

00:33:19.061 --> 00:33:22.895
If you could help me purchase
that thought...

00:33:22.932 --> 00:33:24.365
It's impossible.

00:33:24.400 --> 00:33:27.028
Frane's already had it purged.

00:33:27.069 --> 00:33:29.435
Odd.

00:33:29.472 --> 00:33:31.633
I was certain you possessed it.

00:33:31.674 --> 00:33:33.471
Me?

00:33:37.113 --> 00:33:39.843
Didn't you extract the thought
from B'Elanna as well,

00:33:39.882 --> 00:33:41.975
just after she collided
with Frane?

00:33:42.017 --> 00:33:43.644
What?

00:33:43.686 --> 00:33:46.621
I reevaluated B'Elanna's
memories of the incident.

00:33:46.655 --> 00:33:49.146
She remembers that
you probed her mind.

00:33:49.191 --> 00:33:51.022
She remembers incorrectly.

00:33:51.060 --> 00:33:52.425
Perhaps...

00:33:52.461 --> 00:33:54.861
or perhaps you did
extract that image,

00:33:54.897 --> 00:33:55.955
which would explain

00:33:55.998 --> 00:33:58.592
why that same thought
is still in circulation...

00:33:58.634 --> 00:34:00.192
why it prompted
a murder this morning.

00:34:00.236 --> 00:34:01.225
Enough.

00:34:03.773 --> 00:34:06.264
It's time you gave me
what you promised.

00:34:06.308 --> 00:34:09.038
The only person you'll be
sharing thoughts with tonight

00:34:09.078 --> 00:34:11.069
is the Chief Examiner.

00:34:15.918 --> 00:34:18.409
Where are you going?

00:34:18.454 --> 00:34:19.716
Stand aside.

00:34:19.755 --> 00:34:22.690
Tuvok's taking me into custody.

00:34:22.725 --> 00:34:23.692
No!

00:34:42.645 --> 00:34:44.010
Still no sign of him.

00:34:44.046 --> 00:34:46.105
Try a multiphasic bio-scan.

00:34:46.148 --> 00:34:48.343
We're being hailed, Captain.

00:34:48.384 --> 00:34:49.476
It's Nimira.

00:34:49.518 --> 00:34:51.281
On screen.

00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:54.619
Chief Examiner, have you
had any luck locating Tuvok?

00:34:54.657 --> 00:34:56.682
I'm afraid not.

00:34:56.725 --> 00:34:58.716
I'd like to send a search party.

00:34:58.761 --> 00:35:00.058
I can't allow that.

00:35:00.095 --> 00:35:01.119
Why not?

00:35:01.163 --> 00:35:04.064
We can't risk further violations
of our laws.

00:35:04.099 --> 00:35:05.293
That's ridiculous.

00:35:05.334 --> 00:35:06.301
Tom...

00:35:06.335 --> 00:35:07.359
I really don't think

00:35:07.403 --> 00:35:08.893
we pose a serious threat.

00:35:08.938 --> 00:35:11.304
There's nothing more to discuss.

00:35:11.340 --> 00:35:15.208
Lieutenant Torres will be purged
then returned to you.

00:35:15.244 --> 00:35:18.407
Captain, you can't
let them do that.

00:35:18.447 --> 00:35:20.938
The decision's been made.
I'm sorry.

00:35:31.427 --> 00:35:32.826
Let go of me!

00:35:32.862 --> 00:35:34.454
B'Elanna, please...

00:35:34.563 --> 00:35:35.962
try to relax.

00:35:35.998 --> 00:35:37.465
Oh, you have got to be kidding!

00:35:37.500 --> 00:35:38.592
Sedate her.

00:35:38.634 --> 00:35:39.623
No. Wait!

00:35:57.253 --> 00:35:58.413
Proceed.

00:36:10.165 --> 00:36:12.395
You won't escape punishment
for your crimes.

00:36:12.434 --> 00:36:13.799
Quiet!

00:36:16.004 --> 00:36:18.939
You are responsible for a death.

00:36:18.974 --> 00:36:20.441
I never meant that to happen.

00:36:20.542 --> 00:36:21.907
The old woman begged me
for that thought.

00:36:21.943 --> 00:36:22.910
I had to help her.

00:36:22.944 --> 00:36:23.933
Here.

00:36:27.315 --> 00:36:29.283
You are justifying murder.

00:36:29.317 --> 00:36:30.909
Enough.

00:36:30.952 --> 00:36:32.078
Malin, hold him still.

00:36:35.957 --> 00:36:37.652
Now...

00:36:37.692 --> 00:36:39.683
show me.

00:36:50.705 --> 00:36:52.639
You're holding back.

00:36:52.674 --> 00:36:56.303
I haven't seen
the best of it yet, have I?

00:36:56.344 --> 00:36:57.709
No.

00:36:57.746 --> 00:36:59.111
Then show me.

00:37:01.082 --> 00:37:05.314
If I show you,
will you let me go?

00:37:06.354 --> 00:37:07.946
Yes.

00:37:07.989 --> 00:37:09.513
Come closer.

00:37:12.460 --> 00:37:13.859
Don't be alarmed.

00:37:13.895 --> 00:37:18.594
This will allow you to see
the deepest recesses of my mind.

00:37:18.633 --> 00:37:22.091
My mind... to your mind

00:37:22.137 --> 00:37:23.729
and my thoughts...

00:37:23.772 --> 00:37:25.865
to your thoughts.

00:37:30.245 --> 00:37:31.906
Yes.

00:37:31.947 --> 00:37:33.141
Good.

00:37:38.386 --> 00:37:40.980
This is the side of you
I wanted to know.

00:37:55.203 --> 00:37:59.264
What's... happening?

00:37:59.307 --> 00:38:02.037
We are locked
in a Vulcan mind-meld.

00:38:02.077 --> 00:38:04.671
You don't understand
the truth of violence.

00:38:06.548 --> 00:38:08.175
Its darkness...

00:38:08.216 --> 00:38:09.877
its power!

00:38:26.801 --> 00:38:29.099
Please... stop.

00:38:33.608 --> 00:38:35.769
Increase the electrochemical
displacement,

00:38:35.810 --> 00:38:38.802
but be very careful
with the synaptic potentials.

00:38:38.847 --> 00:38:41.441
One miscalculation
and we could permanently damage

00:38:41.516 --> 00:38:43.416
her cerebral cortex.

00:38:43.451 --> 00:38:45.578
Communications Center
to Chief Examiner Nimira.

00:38:45.620 --> 00:38:47.383
Nimira.

00:38:47.422 --> 00:38:49.856
Captain Janeway insists
on speaking with you.

00:38:49.891 --> 00:38:52.189
She says it's extremely urgent.

00:38:52.227 --> 00:38:55.162
Relay her signal.

00:38:55.196 --> 00:38:56.322
What is it, Captain?

00:38:56.364 --> 00:38:58.093
It's imperative
that you discontinue

00:38:58.133 --> 00:39:01.432
Lieutenant Torres' engramatic
extraction immediately.

00:39:01.469 --> 00:39:03.562
Commander Tuvok
has found new evidence,

00:39:03.605 --> 00:39:06.199
which proves her innocence.

00:39:28.096 --> 00:39:30.291
I hope this interruption
is justified.

00:39:30.331 --> 00:39:33.198
Suspending an engramatic purge
once it's begun

00:39:33.234 --> 00:39:35.259
is highly irregular.

00:39:35.303 --> 00:39:36.429
Then let's not waste
any more time.

00:39:36.538 --> 00:39:37.596
Commander.

00:39:40.075 --> 00:39:41.099
I have discovered

00:39:41.142 --> 00:39:42.837
that Guill and Frane
are responsible

00:39:42.877 --> 00:39:44.435
for the beating
in the marketplace,

00:39:44.546 --> 00:39:46.946
and consequently,
for Talli's murder.

00:39:46.981 --> 00:39:49.108
Guill, the merchant?

00:39:49.150 --> 00:39:50.708
That is correct.

00:39:50.752 --> 00:39:52.686
What possible involvement
could he have?

00:39:52.721 --> 00:39:55.622
It was Frane who acted
on the violent thought.

00:39:55.657 --> 00:39:57.318
That is not in dispute.

00:39:57.358 --> 00:39:59.883
However,
Lieutenant Torres' thought

00:39:59.928 --> 00:40:02.294
was not transferred
accidentally.

00:40:02.330 --> 00:40:03.456
I don't understand.

00:40:03.565 --> 00:40:06.864
When Guill first met
Lieutenant Torres,

00:40:06.901 --> 00:40:10.268
he sensed strong, violent
tendencies within her,

00:40:10.305 --> 00:40:14.605
a potential for mental imagery
which interested him.

00:40:14.642 --> 00:40:16.872
In order to exploit
that potential,

00:40:16.911 --> 00:40:19.971
he conspired with Frane
to provoke B'Elanna.

00:40:20.014 --> 00:40:22.744
They wanted to trigger
a violent thought,

00:40:22.784 --> 00:40:25.651
so they could telepathically
draw it from her mind.

00:40:25.687 --> 00:40:28.588
I can't believe that.

00:40:28.623 --> 00:40:30.887
It is precisely what happened.

00:40:30.925 --> 00:40:33.325
Unfortunately,
they underestimated

00:40:33.361 --> 00:40:34.885
the intensity of the thought.

00:40:34.929 --> 00:40:36.726
It was more powerful

00:40:36.765 --> 00:40:39.063
than anything either of them
had ever experienced.

00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:43.161
As a result, Frane lost control
and attacked the victim.

00:40:43.204 --> 00:40:47.106
Why would peaceful men
like Guill and Frane

00:40:47.142 --> 00:40:50.873
want to subject themselves
to such hostile images?

00:40:50.912 --> 00:40:52.709
My investigation has uncovered

00:40:52.747 --> 00:40:55.511
a rather disturbing side
of Mari society...

00:40:55.617 --> 00:40:57.949
a black market if you will,

00:40:57.986 --> 00:41:01.422
in which many of your citizens
trade in illicit mental imagery.

00:41:01.456 --> 00:41:04.448
Guill is a very prominent figure
in this underground,

00:41:04.559 --> 00:41:07.392
or was, until I brought him
into custody.

00:41:12.400 --> 00:41:14.834
Why would any of my people

00:41:14.869 --> 00:41:17.599
want to indulge
in that kind of behavior?

00:41:17.639 --> 00:41:20.335
Apparently, outlawing
violent thought

00:41:20.375 --> 00:41:22.002
hasn't made it go away.

00:41:22.043 --> 00:41:26.070
All you've done is force people
to share it in back alleys.

00:41:26.114 --> 00:41:28.674
It seems you have
a somewhat more...

00:41:28.716 --> 00:41:31.947
serious problem than the random
thoughts of a single alien.

00:41:35.523 --> 00:41:37.991
Even if I believed you,

00:41:38.026 --> 00:41:40.153
I'm not sure anyone else would.

00:41:40.195 --> 00:41:43.187
Then I suggest you interrogate
Guill yourselves.

00:41:43.231 --> 00:41:44.357
His engramatic record

00:41:44.399 --> 00:41:46.765
will undoubtedly confirm
what I've told you.

00:41:46.801 --> 00:41:48.632
Where is he now?

00:41:48.670 --> 00:41:50.900
We have him confined

00:41:50.939 --> 00:41:52.099
in our brig.

00:41:57.345 --> 00:41:59.404
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:41:59.447 --> 00:42:02.848
Chief Examiner Nimira
has taken custody of Mr. Guill.

00:42:02.884 --> 00:42:04.852
Whether his arrest
will lead to reforms

00:42:04.886 --> 00:42:07.150
in the Mari justice system
is anyone's guess.

00:42:07.188 --> 00:42:09.452
In the meantime, the Doctor
is treating Lieutenant Torres

00:42:09.524 --> 00:42:11.617
and Commander Tuvok.

00:42:11.659 --> 00:42:13.286
Fortunately, the Mari
didn't get very far

00:42:13.328 --> 00:42:14.556
with the procedure.

00:42:14.596 --> 00:42:16.791
You can return to duty,
Lieutenant,

00:42:16.831 --> 00:42:19.197
though perhaps with one
or two fewer violent engrams

00:42:19.234 --> 00:42:20.997
in that fiery head of yours.

00:42:21.035 --> 00:42:22.002
It's all right, Doc.

00:42:22.036 --> 00:42:24.061
There are plenty more
where those came from.

00:42:24.105 --> 00:42:25.970
Duly warned.

00:42:26.007 --> 00:42:27.941
Thanks for getting me
out of there.

00:42:27.976 --> 00:42:30.342
I was merely pursuing the truth.

00:42:30.378 --> 00:42:35.645
So if I was responsible
for passing that thought,

00:42:35.683 --> 00:42:37.344
you would have let them
lobotomize me?

00:42:37.385 --> 00:42:39.478
It is incumbent upon us
to respect the laws

00:42:39.520 --> 00:42:40.987
of the societies we visit.

00:42:41.022 --> 00:42:43.013
So...

00:42:43.057 --> 00:42:47.653
you still a fan
of the Mari legal system?

00:42:47.695 --> 00:42:50.687
My views have been
somewhat modified.

00:42:50.732 --> 00:42:53.030
Then you're not
going to lecture me

00:42:53.067 --> 00:42:54.625
about losing my temper?

00:42:54.669 --> 00:42:56.933
If you must know,
investigating this case

00:42:56.971 --> 00:42:59.201
has given me a new respect
for your inner struggle.

00:42:59.240 --> 00:43:00.434
Really?

00:43:00.475 --> 00:43:02.375
Burdened as you are

00:43:02.410 --> 00:43:04.002
by your primitive
Klingon psyche,

00:43:04.045 --> 00:43:05.342
it is a wonder
you are able to keep

00:43:05.380 --> 00:43:06.711
your violent thoughts
under control

00:43:06.748 --> 00:43:08.272
as much as you do.

00:43:08.316 --> 00:43:11.444
Thanks... I think.

00:43:11.519 --> 00:43:12.679
You're welcome.

00:43:12.720 --> 00:43:16.451
Of course, there are
various Vulcan techniques

00:43:16.491 --> 00:43:18.755
which could help you
increase your self-control.

00:43:18.793 --> 00:43:20.158
You don't say.

00:43:30.738 --> 00:43:31.966
Come in.

00:43:32.006 --> 00:43:33.064
I must speak with you.

00:43:33.107 --> 00:43:34.301
Of course.
Have a seat.

00:43:34.342 --> 00:43:35.309
I prefer to stand.

00:43:35.343 --> 00:43:36.310
I keep forgetting.

00:43:36.344 --> 00:43:37.368
You once encouraged me

00:43:37.412 --> 00:43:38.674
to express my opinions

00:43:38.713 --> 00:43:40.704
if I had something relevant
to say.

00:43:40.748 --> 00:43:42.477
Go right ahead.

00:43:42.583 --> 00:43:45.108
You wish to return this vessel
to the Alpha Quadrant,

00:43:45.153 --> 00:43:47.178
and yet you are following
Starfleet protocol

00:43:47.221 --> 00:43:48.779
regarding first contact.

00:43:48.823 --> 00:43:50.757
The two objectives
are incompatible.

00:43:50.792 --> 00:43:52.191
How so?

00:43:52.226 --> 00:43:54.888
Your philosophy of exploration

00:43:54.929 --> 00:43:56.897
exposes Voyager
to constant risk.

00:43:56.931 --> 00:43:58.831
If you maintain a direct course,

00:43:58.866 --> 00:44:00.663
to Earth and avoid
all extraneous contact

00:44:00.702 --> 00:44:01.669
with alien species,

00:44:01.703 --> 00:44:03.568
it will increase
your chances of survival.

00:44:03.604 --> 00:44:05.572
Well, that would make
a dull ride home.

00:44:05.606 --> 00:44:07.301
Captain?

00:44:07.342 --> 00:44:11.335
We seek out new races
because we want to,

00:44:11.379 --> 00:44:13.404
not because
we're following protocols.

00:44:13.448 --> 00:44:16.611
We have an insatiable curiosity
about the universe.

00:44:16.651 --> 00:44:20.382
Your Chief Engineer and Security
Officer were nearly lost today.

00:44:20.421 --> 00:44:21.718
That is unacceptable.

00:44:21.756 --> 00:44:24.384
To you, maybe,
but not to me or my crew.

00:44:24.425 --> 00:44:27.258
Our experience with the Mari
gave us an insight

00:44:27.295 --> 00:44:29.388
into a culture
we've never encountered.

00:44:31.499 --> 00:44:33.091
But that is irrelevant.

00:44:33.134 --> 00:44:35.830
No.
It's how we gain knowledge.

00:44:37.438 --> 00:44:39.269
Then we are in disagreement.

00:44:39.307 --> 00:44:40.740
Good. I dread the day

00:44:40.775 --> 00:44:42.970
when everyone on this ship
agrees with me.

00:44:43.011 --> 00:44:44.774
I thank you for your opinion,

00:44:44.812 --> 00:44:47.645
but our mission
is not going to change.

00:44:57.692 --> 00:44:59.023
Dismissed.
